    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "SAN FRANCISCO FROM THE PACIFIC, GOLDEN GATE, G. G. BRIDGE, BUSINESS DISTRICT,\n41\n8A-H3156\nSAN FRANCISCO OAKLAND BAY BRIDGE, OAKLAND, BERKELEY, ALAMEDA AND EAST BAY CITIES IN DISTANCE",
      "Looking in from the Pacific through the\nGolden Gate one finds San Francisco linked\nNorth and East with two stupendous bridges;\none across the Golden Gate entrance to San\nFrancisco Bay, a $35,000,000.00 structure on\nwhich one single span\nmeasures 4,200 tt.,\ncompleting a connecting link with all northern\ncounties and the famous Redwood Empire.\nThe $77,000,000.00 San Francisco-Oakland Bay\nBridge, shown in the distance, joins Oakland,\nBerkeley, Alameda and other East Bay Cities\nthus forming a Metropolitan Area unsurpassed\nfor continued Commercial Progress.\nPLACE\nONE CENT\nSTAMP\nHERE\nSTANLEY A. PILTZ COMPANY, SAN\nFRANCISCO, CALIF.\nPOST CARD\n\"Pictorial Wanderland\"\nSENIE\n41\n2012.149.0475"
